A monad in \K  consists of

a 0-cell x, the object the monad acts on;

an endo-1-cell t : \K 1{x}{x};

a multiplication 2-cell \mu  : \hc {t}{t} \Rightarrow  t;

a unit 2-cell \eta  : 1_{x} \Rightarrow  t;

such that \mu  is associative: the following diagram of
     2-cells commutes in \K 1{x}{x}, where the top
     map is the associator that rebrackets the threefold composite:





